\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Brother man, fold to thy 
\par heart thy brother!
\par Where pity dwells, the peace of 
\par God is there;
\par To worship rightly is to love
\par each other,
\par Each smile a hymn, each
\par kindly deed a prayer.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. For he whom Jesus loved
\par hath truly spoken:
\par The holier worship which He 
\par designs to bless
\par Restores the lost, and binds 
\par the spirit broken,
\par And feeds the widow and
\par the fatherless.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Follow with reverent steps 
\par the great example
\par Of Him whose holy work 
\par was doing good;
\par So shall the wide earth seem
\par our Father's temple,
\par Each loving life a 
\par psalm  of gratitude.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Then shall all shackles fall;
\par the stormy  clangour
\par Of wild war- music o'er the 
\par earth shall cease;
\par Love shall tread out the baleful
\par fire of anger,
\par And in its ashes plant the 
\par tree of peace.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

